    <briefdescription>
<para>Composite pattern. </para>    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The typical use of this class is: <programlisting><codeline><highlight class="keyword">class<sp/></highlight><highlight class="normal">CompositeFoo<sp/>:<sp/></highlight><highlight class="keyword">public</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>Composite&lt;Foo&gt;<sp/>{</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>...</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">};</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting> which causes CompositeFoo to inherit from Foo and provides it with methods for adding components. Of course, any abstract Foo interface must still be implemented. </para>    </detaileddescription>
